                            <comment id="15326236" author="githubbot" created="Sun, 12 Jun 2016 07:27:48 +0000"  >&lt;p&gt;Github user felizbear commented on the issue:&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;    &lt;a href=&quot;https://github.com/apache/zeppelin/pull/978&quot; class=&quot;external-link&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot; rel=&quot;nofollow noopener&quot;&gt;https://github.com/apache/zeppelin/pull/978&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;    Also, I would recommend modify `ng-disabled` of search form in navbar like this:&lt;br/&gt;
    ```&lt;br/&gt;
    ng-disabled=&quot;!navbar.connected || !searchTerm&quot;&lt;br/&gt;
    ```&lt;br/&gt;
    so it doesn&apos;t fire when there is an empty field&lt;/p&gt;</comment>
                            <comment id="15326241" author="githubbot" created="Sun, 12 Jun 2016 07:31:19 +0000"  >&lt;p&gt;Github user felizbear commented on the issue:&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;    &lt;a href=&quot;https://github.com/apache/zeppelin/pull/978&quot; class=&quot;external-link&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot; rel=&quot;nofollow noopener&quot;&gt;https://github.com/apache/zeppelin/pull/978&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;    Also, I think you will have to clean up scope after you clear the search field value. To see what I mean do the following:&lt;br/&gt;
    1. Search for something, e.g. `bankText`&lt;br/&gt;
    2. Navigate away from the search result page (search field now is empty)&lt;br/&gt;
    3. Search again with the empty search field&lt;br/&gt;
    4. See `bankText` results again (expected to see an empty page or even have search field disabled like I suggested above)&lt;/p&gt;</comment>
